WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:00.300
[ Watch on KissFlix.co ]

2
00:00.400 --> 00:05.320
I...

3
00:05.320 --> 00:06.440
I like Serizawa.

4
00:06.440 --> 00:09.530
From now on, I'll match your speed.

5
00:09.530 --> 00:11.130
My speed?

6
00:11.130 --> 00:14.490
So, that's what this is all about.

7
00:14.490 --> 00:16.340
He said he has a crush on someone.

8
00:16.340 --> 00:18.820
He's been crushing on them since his first year.

9
00:18.820 --> 00:22.150
Woah, he's so loyal.

10
00:28.340 --> 00:32.190
I wonder who Serizawa's crush is.

11
00:32.190 --> 00:33.830
Let me see your hand.

12
00:37.630 --> 00:42.470
Of course a guy like him would have a dazzling romance.

13
00:42.470 --> 00:44.240
Sorry!

14
00:45.180 --> 00:46.780
Matsuno?

15
00:46.780 --> 00:49.320
Suzuki...

16
00:49.320 --> 00:52.680
Sorry about that. Here, use this.

17
00:54.420 --> 00:56.110
Thanks.

18
00:57.430 --> 01:00.730
You don't need to give that back to me.

19
01:06.890 --> 01:08.680
Suzuki.

20
01:14.200 --> 01:18.160
Never mind.

21
01:24.630 --> 01:26.910
Suzuki?

22
01:26.910 --> 01:28.690
Is everything okay?

23
01:29.840 --> 01:32.210
Yeah, thanks.

24
01:32.210 --> 01:36.470
Was he trying to make up with you?

25
01:36.470 --> 01:40.680
No. Things are still pretty awkward between us.

26
01:41.590 --> 01:44.330
We used to be best friends

27
01:44.330 --> 01:47.120
back in freshman year though.

28
01:48.730 --> 01:52.600
But I'm your bestest friend now, right?

29
01:52.600 --> 01:54.180
That's something I won't budge on.

30
01:54.180 --> 01:55.350
Personal space!

31
01:55.350 --> 02:00.720
If anything, I wanted to be friends back in freshman year, too.

32
02:07.680 --> 02:13.890
I also wish we'd known each other earlier.

33
02:15.120 --> 02:17.430
Right, I almost forgot to ask.

34
02:17.430 --> 02:19.720
Wanna go to the beach with me?

35
02:19.720 --> 02:21.710
- The beach? - Yeah.

36
02:21.710 --> 02:25.160
Let's go and make summer memories together.

37
03:14.680 --> 03:16.470
The beach...

38
03:20.100 --> 03:22.500
[Episode 8]

39
03:22.500 --> 03:25.010
Summer memories...

40
03:26.760 --> 03:28.460
Suzuki!

41
03:32.440 --> 03:34.450
Over here!

42
03:36.420 --> 03:40.260
Together, with just Serizawa.

43
03:54.240 --> 03:56.910
I guess not, huh?

44
03:57.700 --> 04:00.360
Is that Suzupi?

45
04:00.360 --> 04:02.660
Hey, what's up!

46
04:02.660 --> 04:04.820
You came to join us!

47
04:04.820 --> 04:06.950
Awesome!

48
04:06.950 --> 04:09.080
Come on, let's go!

49
04:09.080 --> 04:12.750
Yeah.

50
04:12.750 --> 04:16.110
Three, two, one...

51
04:20.700 --> 04:23.110
Looking good!

52
04:23.110 --> 04:25.250
Hold on.

53
04:25.250 --> 04:28.930
No one told me the girls were joining, too.

54
04:28.930 --> 04:32.610
Extroverted popular kids are built different.

55
04:33.420 --> 04:39.060
Maybe one of them is Serizawa's crush.

56
04:39.990 --> 04:41.580
Is it Miyamoto?

57
04:41.580 --> 04:43.560
Takahashi?

58
04:43.560 --> 04:45.500
Sakuraba?

59
04:45.500 --> 04:49.500
No, she's Saeki's girlfriend.

60
04:49.500 --> 04:51.110
Suzuki.

61
04:53.160 --> 04:55.630
Why are you staring at the girls?

62
04:55.630 --> 04:57.390
No, I...

63
04:57.390 --> 04:59.100
Come join the rest of us.

64
05:02.460 --> 05:05.220
You aren't gonna take a dip?

65
05:05.220 --> 05:08.810
Well...

66
05:08.810 --> 05:11.280
You know.

67
05:11.280 --> 05:13.890
Everyone else looks so dazzling, so...

68
05:15.020 --> 05:17.180
Hey, don't exclude yourself.

69
05:18.580 --> 05:21.440
We're making summer memories together, right?

70
05:23.780 --> 05:25.580
- Yeah. - Come on.

71
06:01.440 --> 06:03.010
Huh?

72
06:03.010 --> 06:04.970
You're out.

73
06:04.970 --> 06:09.670
- Serizawa! - That's your fault for just standing there.

74
06:09.670 --> 06:11.780
You asked for it!

75
06:12.890 --> 06:15.020
I hate to admit it.

76
06:15.020 --> 06:17.470
But whenever I'm with Serizawa,

77
06:17.470 --> 06:22.900
he always ropes me into his schemes.

78
06:36.800 --> 06:39.180
I can't deny it.

79
06:40.850 --> 06:43.890
I...

80
06:43.890 --> 06:45.190
Around you go!

81
06:45.190 --> 06:48.110
Serizawa! Pause!

82
06:48.110 --> 06:52.110
Stop it!

83
06:52.110 --> 06:54.330
Stop spinning me!

84
07:04.160 --> 07:05.780
- Reon. - Yeah?

85
07:06.870 --> 07:09.000
- Let me have a sip. - Huh?

86
07:09.710 --> 07:11.470
That's not a sip.

87
07:11.470 --> 07:15.390
- Cheapskate. - Give it back.

88
07:19.140 --> 07:21.460
More! More!

89
07:23.210 --> 07:24.960
There!

90
07:24.960 --> 07:27.330
Cover his legs.

91
07:27.330 --> 07:29.410
What's up?

92
07:34.180 --> 07:39.070
Does Serizawa have a crush on...

93
07:41.030 --> 07:42.690
Here.

94
07:42.690 --> 07:44.740
Huh? You sure?

95
07:47.790 --> 07:49.480
Actually, 10,000 yen for the bottle.

96
07:49.480 --> 07:51.280
That's too expensive.

97
07:52.380 --> 07:54.270
- Thanks. - Anytime.

98
07:59.890 --> 08:02.190
You having fun?

99
08:02.190 --> 08:03.680
Yeah.

100
08:05.770 --> 08:11.120
I just wonder if the others actually want me here.

101
08:11.120 --> 08:12.990
Of course they do.

102
08:12.990 --> 08:18.260
You might not realize it, but we all enjoy your company.

103
08:20.800 --> 08:23.020
Thanks.

104
08:23.020 --> 08:25.940
You're a nice guy, Takeuchi.

105
08:25.940 --> 08:28.960
Nah, I wouldn't say that.

106
08:31.310 --> 08:33.040
Say, can I ask something?

107
08:35.090 --> 08:38.760
Have you all been friends since freshman year?

108
08:38.760 --> 08:41.350
Yeah.

109
08:41.350 --> 08:45.060
I was in a different class though.

110
08:46.160 --> 08:48.050
I see.

111
08:49.350 --> 08:51.210
Then...

112
08:52.610 --> 08:55.590
You two are drinking ramune?

113
08:55.590 --> 08:57.360
No fair!

114
08:57.360 --> 09:00.190
Where's our share?

115
09:00.190 --> 09:02.410
Get your own bottles.

116
09:02.410 --> 09:04.650
- The vendor's over there. - Rude!

117
09:04.650 --> 09:06.540
Serizawa, could you get us some?

118
09:06.540 --> 09:07.590
Why me?

119
09:07.590 --> 09:10.430
We're all thirsty, me included.

120
09:10.430 --> 09:12.840
Please?

121
09:13.910 --> 09:16.090
Fine.

122
09:17.130 --> 09:20.140
Suzuki, you're coming with.

123
09:24.660 --> 09:26.400
Suzuki?

124
09:35.180 --> 09:37.640
- Come on. - Huh?

125
09:40.560 --> 09:43.620
- Serizawa? - Yeah?

126
09:43.620 --> 09:46.250
You're still holding my hand.

127
09:46.250 --> 09:49.010
I know.

128
09:50.280 --> 09:52.490
Are you mad?

129
09:52.490 --> 09:54.290
No.

130
09:55.090 --> 09:58.720
Why were you staring so hard at Reon?

131
09:58.720 --> 10:05.760
Because you two seemed like good friends.

132
10:05.760 --> 10:07.580
So what?

133
10:11.390 --> 10:15.140
Wait, were you jealous of her?

134
10:15.140 --> 10:18.240
No. That's not it.

135
10:18.240 --> 10:20.900
To tell you the truth,

136
10:21.940 --> 10:24.880
I overheard our upperclassmen talking, and...

137
10:27.110 --> 10:31.940
They said you had a crush on someone.

138
10:31.940 --> 10:33.460
Huh?

139
10:35.040 --> 10:39.810
I thought maybe it was Miyamoto.

140
10:39.810 --> 10:42.440
No, it's not.

141
10:42.440 --> 10:44.610
Then is it Takahashi?

142
10:44.610 --> 10:46.420
No.

143
10:47.250 --> 10:48.700
Sakuraba?

144
10:48.700 --> 10:52.640
Saeki's girlfriend? Of course not.

145
10:52.640 --> 10:54.810
Right, I thought so.

146
10:56.360 --> 11:01.530
But I do have a crush.

147
11:04.300 --> 11:06.100
You haven't noticed?

148
11:06.770 --> 11:09.870
We're always together, my crush and I.

149
11:09.870 --> 11:11.350
Really?

150
11:12.650 --> 11:14.410
They're a nice person.

151
11:14.410 --> 11:17.410
Very cute, kind,

152
11:17.410 --> 11:19.250
and hardworking, too.

153
11:22.600 --> 11:26.260
Unfortunately, they're also very dense.

154
11:26.260 --> 11:29.280
We were finally placed in the same class this year,

155
11:29.280 --> 11:34.490
and I've been making moves, but they still haven't noticed.

156
11:38.060 --> 11:42.880
That's another reason why they're so cute.

157
11:42.880 --> 11:44.800
And I love them all the more for it.

158
11:51.520 --> 11:53.100
So?

159
11:54.040 --> 11:57.390
Can you guess who I'm talking about?

160
12:09.400 --> 12:10.950
More?

161
12:10.950 --> 12:12.860
You're definitely lying.

162
12:12.860 --> 12:14.240
It needs fuel!

163
12:14.240 --> 12:15.730
How about that?

164
12:15.730 --> 12:17.010
Give me the tongs.

165
12:17.010 --> 12:18.680
You're not doing it right.

166
12:18.680 --> 12:21.680
What?

167
12:22.600 --> 12:26.380
I had no idea who he was talking about.

168
12:26.380 --> 12:32.310
Honestly, I was too nervous to really process what he was saying.

169
12:32.310 --> 12:35.080
How hasn't he caught on by now?

170
12:36.390 --> 12:39.430
He's the king of being dense.

171
12:39.430 --> 12:42.150
I gave him plenty of hints to work with!

172
12:42.150 --> 12:46.340
This is Suzuki we're talking about.

173
12:46.340 --> 12:48.250
Hints won't do the trick.

174
12:48.250 --> 12:51.450
Just say it outright already.

175
12:51.450 --> 12:53.180
Follow my lead.

176
12:53.180 --> 12:55.740
- "Suzuki! I..." - Shh!

177
12:55.740 --> 12:57.740
You think it's so easy.

178
12:57.740 --> 13:01.800
I've been inching closer to him since freshman year,

179
13:01.800 --> 13:04.890
only to finally become friends with him.

180
13:04.890 --> 13:07.810
I won't let Suzuki get away.

181
13:07.810 --> 13:09.610
Terrifying.

182
13:09.610 --> 13:13.010
Still, I get how you feel.

183
13:13.010 --> 13:18.530
Confessing could put the other in an awkward spot.

184
13:18.530 --> 13:20.660
Exactly.

185
13:20.660 --> 13:24.080
If only I knew that Suzuki

186
13:24.760 --> 13:26.960
felt anything for me.

187
13:27.830 --> 13:32.230
I do wonder what he thinks of me.

188
13:34.810 --> 13:37.350
No way. Really?

189
13:37.350 --> 13:39.600
Who is it?

190
13:39.600 --> 13:41.940
Who is Serizawa's crush?

191
13:41.940 --> 13:43.850
Suzuki.

192
13:43.850 --> 13:45.920
Thanks for joining us.

193
13:45.920 --> 13:47.120
No problem.

194
13:47.120 --> 13:50.410
I like cooking, anyway.

195
13:50.410 --> 13:53.010
I meant at the beach today.

196
13:53.010 --> 13:54.430
- Huh? - By the way,

197
13:54.430 --> 13:57.690
how'd you become friends with Serizawa?

198
13:58.340 --> 14:01.620
I know we asked before, but we never got an answer.

199
14:01.620 --> 14:04.820
Was there something that brought you two together?

200
14:06.710 --> 14:10.750
Actually...

201
14:10.750 --> 14:13.780
it was because I like BL.

202
14:13.780 --> 14:16.030
BL?

203
14:16.030 --> 14:17.980
Yeah.

204
14:17.980 --> 14:22.320
Right. I forgot Serizawa's a BL fan.

205
14:22.320 --> 14:23.850
You knew?

206
14:23.850 --> 14:26.230
Yeah. He read it often during freshman year.

207
14:26.230 --> 14:29.610
I've read a bit, too. It's interesting!

208
14:29.610 --> 14:31.430
Yeah.

209
14:31.430 --> 14:35.640
He started reading it totally out of the blue.

210
14:35.640 --> 14:36.970
Huh?

211
14:36.970 --> 14:38.600
Yeah, I remember.

212
14:38.600 --> 14:40.150
He said he picked it up

213
14:40.150 --> 14:44.000
because of his crush.

214
14:45.260 --> 14:47.430
His crush...

215
14:48.230 --> 14:50.510
Hold on.

216
14:50.510 --> 14:52.960
Doesn't that mean...

217
14:53.700 --> 14:55.370
Seriously?

218
14:55.370 --> 14:57.780
That's why?

219
15:05.850 --> 15:07.860
I don't understand.

220
15:11.810 --> 15:13.790
Tastes like protein.

221
15:13.790 --> 15:16.000
Here, try a bite.

222
15:16.000 --> 15:18.050
- Away you go. - Woah!

223
15:18.050 --> 15:20.340
- Now that the pest is gone. - Yeah.

224
15:20.340 --> 15:22.570
Here.

225
15:22.570 --> 15:23.980
Ready?

226
15:23.980 --> 15:25.430
Go for it.

227
15:25.430 --> 15:27.710
Smells good.

228
15:28.880 --> 15:32.280
In other words, Serizawa's crush...

229
15:32.280 --> 15:35.660
He's been crushing on them since his first year.

230
15:35.660 --> 15:39.350
is someone he met in freshman year.

231
15:40.000 --> 15:44.470
But they only became classmates this year.

232
15:44.470 --> 15:46.090
You haven't noticed?

233
15:46.090 --> 15:49.230
We're always together, my crush and I.

234
15:49.230 --> 15:51.360
His crush is also always with him,

235
15:51.360 --> 15:55.000
and is a fellow BL fan?

236
15:55.000 --> 15:59.330
Who could it be? No one fits the bill...

237
15:59.330 --> 16:02.090
Suzuki, are you eating?

238
16:02.090 --> 16:03.390
Here.

239
16:03.390 --> 16:05.350
Hold it right there!

240
16:06.980 --> 16:09.250
- What? - Here.

241
16:09.250 --> 16:11.540
Take the one I grilled.

242
16:11.540 --> 16:14.060
Who cares who grilled it? It's all the same.

243
16:14.060 --> 16:15.560
Is not.

244
16:15.560 --> 16:18.170
Meat is always grilled with love.

245
16:18.170 --> 16:20.040
- Love? - Love.

246
16:20.040 --> 16:21.960
- Okay... - Here.

247
16:22.850 --> 16:24.610
Thanks.

248
16:26.130 --> 16:29.020
You're not making any sense.

249
16:34.090 --> 16:35.980
Wait a second...

250
16:36.660 --> 16:39.620
I want to read your work.

251
16:39.620 --> 16:41.650
I'm a fellow BL lover, after all.

252
16:41.650 --> 16:42.770
You too?

253
16:42.770 --> 16:45.990
I've been reading the stuff since before Serizawa.

254
16:45.990 --> 16:50.230
I was in a different class though.

255
16:50.230 --> 16:52.330
Is his crush...

256
16:52.330 --> 16:53.790
Suzuki?

257
16:53.790 --> 16:55.560
Are you not hungry?

258
16:56.790 --> 16:58.460
No, I am.

259
16:59.510 --> 17:03.460
Takeuchi, you and Serizawa went to the same middle school, right?

260
17:03.460 --> 17:06.180
Yeah.

261
17:06.180 --> 17:09.360
Were you two ever in the same class?

262
17:10.510 --> 17:16.520
No. This year's the first time we're together.

263
17:17.450 --> 17:21.230
But we really only became friends

264
17:21.230 --> 17:23.860
in freshman year of high school.

265
17:23.860 --> 17:27.010
We were both on the library committee.

266
17:29.370 --> 17:30.950
Why?

267
17:32.010 --> 17:33.750
No reason.

268
17:36.210 --> 17:38.070
Crap, my marshmallow's burning.

269
17:38.070 --> 17:41.000
Takeuchi, help! Hurry!

270
17:41.000 --> 17:44.050
Why in the world is it burning?

271
17:44.860 --> 17:47.450
Yikes! Help!

272
17:47.450 --> 17:49.220
Get it out of there!

273
17:49.220 --> 17:51.370
Fan it.

274
17:51.370 --> 17:53.180
There is one person

275
17:54.160 --> 17:57.550
who completely fits the bill.

276
17:58.920 --> 17:59.940
Woah!

277
17:59.940 --> 18:03.350
There it goes!

278
18:13.930 --> 18:17.050
Cute!

279
18:23.770 --> 18:28.150
I'm living my youth!

280
18:43.830 --> 18:47.300
I get it. Anyone would like Takeuchi.

281
18:47.300 --> 18:51.760
He's kind, confident,

282
18:51.760 --> 18:54.270
and just a good guy overall.

283
18:55.280 --> 18:56.920
Still...

284
18:59.250 --> 19:02.370
Serizawa, let me light mine.

285
19:19.550 --> 19:22.610
Serizawa.

286
19:23.840 --> 19:27.200
What am I supposed to do?

287
19:27.200 --> 19:32.890
My chest hurts so much.

288
19:34.840 --> 19:36.740
Those two are different!

289
19:36.740 --> 19:39.520
- Are they? - Yeah!

290
19:46.740 --> 19:48.780
Excuse me.

291
19:49.610 --> 19:51.200
Hup.

292
19:52.410 --> 19:55.890
What's up, Suzuki?

293
19:56.560 --> 19:58.920
Let's enjoy the fireworks together.

294
20:00.200 --> 20:01.850
Right.

295
20:02.780 --> 20:07.320
Here, take one.

296
20:07.320 --> 20:10.110
- A sparkler? - Yeah.

297
20:10.110 --> 20:13.170
It'll make for a great summer memory, don't you think?

298
20:15.550 --> 20:18.480
Did you know?

299
20:18.480 --> 20:22.490
If your sparkler lasts the entire stick,

300
20:22.490 --> 20:25.170
your wish will come true.

301
20:25.170 --> 20:26.550
A wish?

302
20:26.550 --> 20:27.960
Yeah.

303
20:27.960 --> 20:31.620
I'll tell you mine.

304
20:31.620 --> 20:37.110
I wish my crush will like me forever.

305
20:52.720 --> 20:54.210
Hold it right there!

306
20:54.210 --> 20:57.110
Meat is always grilled with love.

307
20:57.110 --> 20:59.640
- Love? - Love.

308
21:06.540 --> 21:08.680
So close.

309
21:09.990 --> 21:12.630
Your turn.

310
21:12.630 --> 21:14.110
Here.

311
21:15.980 --> 21:20.230
You aren't going to make a wish?

312
21:22.090 --> 21:24.190
No.

313
21:24.190 --> 21:26.470
I'll pass.

314
21:39.080 --> 21:42.550
We're going out as a class after this. Wanna join?

315
21:42.550 --> 21:45.560
No matter how many times you lost heart,

316
21:45.560 --> 21:48.610
you still continued to write.

317
21:48.610 --> 21:50.560
That's seriously amazing, you know?

318
21:50.560 --> 21:52.920
Next time, at least say a quick bye, okay?

319
21:52.920 --> 21:55.300
I'm a huge fan of BL, too.

320
21:55.300 --> 21:57.810
What's so wrong about that?

321
21:57.810 --> 22:00.360
See?

322
22:00.360 --> 22:02.040
I told you they wouldn't judge.

323
22:02.040 --> 22:03.890
Thanks, Serizawa.

324
22:03.890 --> 22:07.500
Accept the fact

325
22:07.500 --> 22:09.750
that I think you're awesome.

326
22:10.670 --> 22:12.710
You're adorable, Suzuki.

327
22:12.710 --> 22:16.470
You're at the top of my list of people I want at my side.

328
22:20.290 --> 22:24.900
I like Serizawa after all.

329
22:26.830 --> 22:30.080
What about you, Suzuki?

330
22:30.080 --> 22:31.950
Do you have a crush on anyone?

331
22:33.220 --> 22:36.330
That's why...

332
22:39.780 --> 22:43.490
No, I don't.

333
22:48.900 --> 22:50.600
I see.

334
22:54.020 --> 22:59.510
I'll choose to root for Serizawa.

335
